    "updated_at": "2025-02-05T18:59:00Z",
    "body": "That's a good insight. It suggests that if there is an issue, it probably has something to do with PySCF and not qiskit-addon-sqd. What version of PySCF were you using to reproduce that value? I was using 2.5.0, but the latest version is 2.8.0. The issue also can be reproduced on 2.8.0. I think I will go ahead and submit a bug report to the PySCF GitHub. \n\nSomething I would note is that with the PySCF code snippet, I can't reproduce the -1.47 result. The fact that SQD seems to also sometimes produce such a low accuracy result, even when given way more measurements than is necessary to get a selected ci problem which spans its entire Hilbert space, is a bit odd. There may be two separate issues hiding here. (Or I am making two different mistakes.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
