    "body": "\n\n\n\n> That's a good insight. It suggests that if there is an issue, it probably has something to do with PySCF and not qiskit-addon-sqd. What version of PySCF were you using to reproduce that value? I was using 2.5.0, but the latest version is 2.8.0. The issue also can be reproduced on 2.8.0. I think I will go ahead and submit a bug report to the PySCF GitHub.\n> \n> Something I would note is that with the PySCF code snippet, I can't reproduce the -1.47 result. The fact that SQD seems to also sometimes produce such a low accuracy result, even when given way more measurements than is necessary to get a selected ci problem which spans its entire Hilbert space, is a bit odd. There may be two separate issues hiding here. (Or I am making two different mistakes.)\n\nCould you verify translating your integrals to MO basis solves this particular issue (even though we didn't fully track down the reason for the two different values occurring when running w AO integrals)",
